# BlindScore

Stack: DeepSpace SDK (`deepspace`, `deepspace/worker`), Cloudflare Workers, Durable Objects, React 19, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4.

Server actions live in `src/actions/index.ts`. Schemas live in `src/schemas/blindscore.ts`. The worker entry is `worker.ts`.

## Constraints

1. Clients never write BlindScore collections. `createCandidate`, `joinPanel`, `submitScorecard`, `forceReveal`, and `generateDebrief` own every write.

2. Scores live in `scorecards` (author-only, `read: 'own'` for member and admin) and in the single `reveals` row. `submissions` has no score columns.

3. Identity comes from `ctx.userId` only. Do not set `userBound` on `interviewerId`.

4. Reveal creates one `reveals` record with `recordId === candidateId`, then updates candidate status. Do not describe those two writes as one transaction.

5. The debrief uses `createDeepSpaceAI` and `generateText` inside `generateDebrief`. Do not put an API key in the repo. The model writes prose; `computeStats` does the arithmetic. The model must not recommend hire or no-hire.

6. Strict TypeScript. No `any`. No new dependencies without asking.
